# Not copied into any layer — the Dockerfile names the paths it needs rather than
# doing `COPY . .` — but still uploaded to the daemon as build context on every build.
# .git alone is several megabytes, and there is no reason to send it or the deployment
# manifests to a builder that will never read them.
